cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Decision Model Guard in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Decision Model Guard: guardrails for decision models"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Patronus Protect"
    website: "https://patronus.studio"
repository-code: "https://github.com/patronus-protect/decision-model-guard"
url: "https://github.com/patronus-protect/decision-model-guard"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
abstract: >-
  Decision Model Guard protects decision models (Jev-like models, classifiers and LLM judges) from text inside the
  content that steers their answer. It scans untrusted content, runs an erase-and-check steering gate around any
  decision model, checks long content window by window, flags answers that change with the input format or the option
  wording, abstains with conformal coverage guarantees, and audits a model's robustness with and without the guard.
keywords:
  - decision models
  - guardrails
  - prompt injection
  - decision steering
  - LLM judge
  - AI security
  - conformal prediction
